<title>UK: BFI down four at 1,454, but grain trade increases.</title>
<headline>BFI down four at 1,454, but grain trade increases.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Baltic Freight Index (BFI) fell four points to 1,454 on Thursday, although a considerably increased volume of grain trading was seen.</p>
<p>Brokers also reported fresh enquiry, especially from South America. Transatlantic panamax rates were broadly unchanged, but handysizes have scored gains from Argentina, Brazil, and the Continent.</p>
<p>The baltic handy index was up two at 1,081.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom 44 171 542 8080</p>
